WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
By contact height we divide balls into low, middle and high.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:10.580
Middle height is waist height, the easiest height for beginners to get started with.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.560
Our earlier lessons all used this height as the reference, so we won't cover it separately here.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.300
First, how to deal with low balls.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:24.280
The contact point of a low ball is much lower than the waist height we started with, usually knee height or below.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.680
If we don't lower ourselves, we end up scooping the ball while standing up.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000 line:10%
Common mistake

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:37.590
Use your legs to adjust: lower your weight and the height of the backswing.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.830
However high the ball is, that's how high you set the racket.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.470
After the split step, quickly crouch as low as the ball and settle into a low, stable stance.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.830
Now imagine a high-speed train coming at you: brace your body, meet the force and drive it back.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.060
When you hit, stay down; don't stand up mid-stroke. Stay low through the whole stroke.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000 line:10%
Common mistake

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:06.900
Once you have these details, we put them into the forehand and backhand framework and practise each with the ball machine.
